DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("(sin(x))^2+3*(x/10)+5");
$fun_1 = Formula("(7/((ln(x))))/3");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("{-10, -3, -1, 6, 10} U {-3, 9}");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("(1, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-10, -3, -1, 6, 10}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (({-10, -3, -1, 6, 10} U {-3, 9} - ((-infinity, infinity) - (1, infinity))) U {-3, 9}))");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(-infinity, 16] - ((-infinity, infinity) - (-infinity, 16]) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (-infinity, 16])");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("(-infinity, 16] U ([2, 14]) U {-3, 5, 10}");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("[2, 14] U [2, 14] U [2, 14]");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`3+15.85-17/10`]? [_____]{17.15}
---

[`0.99+5.48+2+5.69/5.4`] is equal to [_____]{Real(9.5237037037)}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | 2 \leq x \leq 14\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \leq 16\}`]
- [`C = \{-3, 5, 10\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cap B \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`B \cup (A) \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`A \cup A \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-3, 9\}`]
- [`B = \{-10, -3, -1, 6, 10\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x > 0\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`C \cap B \cap ((B \cup A \cap C) \cup A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -2, -6, -4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -3, -1, -8 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-3, -1, -8>") . Compute("<-2, -6, -4>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-2, -6, -4>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-3, -1, -8>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-3, -1, -8>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-2, -6, -4>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-2, -6, -4>") . Compute("<-3, -1, -8>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 4, -3, 8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 1, -3, -5 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -9, -3, -8 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-9, -3, -8>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<1, -3, -5>"))}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-9, -3, -8>") x Compute("<4, -3, 8>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<4, -3, 8>"))}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>9)}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>2)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
